    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 1.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.5-2"/> gif hit hwa do, forgylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.3"/> ðone þeof be his were — ⁊ ne beo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.6-2"/> þam þeofe no<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.2"/> ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.7-2"/> geþingodre — oþþe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.8"/> hine be þ[am] geladie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.5"/> hit hwá dó, forgylde ðone ðeof be his were—⁊ ne beo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.6"/> ðam ðeofe na ðe geðingodre—oððe hine be ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.7"/> geladige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hit hwa dó forgeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> þone þeof be his were — ⁊ ne sie þam þeof<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> na ðe geðingodere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> — oððe hine be ðam ladige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="151" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis hoc presumat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.8-2"/>, persoluat ipsum furem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.9"/> secundum weram suam — et non sit ipsi furi remissius in aliquo — uel ita perneget<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.10"/> (se adlegiet).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="126" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ gif hit hwa do, forgylde ðone þeof be his were—⁊ ne beo<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_1-1.attnote.fn.6"/> þam þeofe no ðe geþingodre—oþþe hine be þam geladie<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-1.attnote.fn.7"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="151" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn es [das Schonen] jemand thut, bezahle er den Dieb durch dessen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.de.1"/> Wergeld — und für den Dieb sei dadurch [die Strafe] keineswegs mehr herabgehandelt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.de.2"/> — oder er schwöre sich rein [durch Eid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-1.lnote.de.3"/>] im Werthe von jenem [Wergeld].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone does it [the sparing], let him pay for the thief with the thief's wergild — and for the thief [the penalty] is not thereby bargained down at all — or let him clear himself [by oath] to the value of that [wergild].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="127" ed="#attenborough"/>And if anyone does spare such a thief, he shall either pay for him to the amount of his<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_1-1.attnote.n.1"/> wergeld—though in that case the thief shall not be any the less liable to punishment—or clear himself [of the accusation] by an oath of equivalent value.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="418" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone does spare one, he is to pay for the thief with his wergild—and the thief is to be no nearer a settlement on that account—or to clear himself by an oath of that amount.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Duns_6-2">Duns 6.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="367"><label>likely reference to</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_36">Ine 36</ref> <quote>Likely references include [...] ii Æthelstan §1.1 (Ine §37)</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif hwa hit dó <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif hwa hit dó Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o. h. be þ[am <hi rend="italic">verschnitten</hi>] gel. <hi rend="italic">am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o. h. be þ[am cropped] gel. in the margin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-met <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-met K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">furum, <hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> furtum <hi rend="italic">M;</hi> furtum <hi rend="italic">HkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">furum, altered to furtum M; furtum HkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond;</hi> (<hi rend="italic">eingeklammertes</hi>) <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">before the bracket Lond; (the bracketed words) the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Schmid 575, Cosack (<hi rend="italic">Eideshelfer</hi> 34) verstehen Wergeld des Begünstigers. Dann läse As <hi rend="italic">hine</hi> (‘sich’, nicht <hi rend="italic">þone þeof</hi>) oder <hi rend="italic">his agne</hi>. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> vielmehr 1, 4. 2, 2 und Ine 36; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Begünstigung 3. Besonders II 20, 8 zeigt, dass sich der Reinigungseid nach dem Wergeld des Begünstigten richtet; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Eidesschwere 2 b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Schmid 575 and Cosack (<hi rend="italic">Eideshelfer</hi> 34) understand the wergild of the abettor. In that case As would have <hi rend="italic">hine</hi> (‘himself’, not <hi rend="italic">þone þeof</hi>) or <hi rend="italic">his agne</hi>. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> rather 1, 4. 2, 2 and Ine 36; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Begünstigung 3. II 20, 8 in particular shows that the oath of exculpation is governed by the wergild of the person abetted; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Eidesschwere 2 b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diese Halbzeile vielleicht aus Ine 22</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This half-line perhaps from Ine 22</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Es schwören also nicht beim gemeinfreien (bzw. adligen) Diebe immer gleich viele freie (bzw. adlige) Helfer, sondern die Eideswerte der Schwörenden summiert gleichen dem Wergeld des Diebes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Thus it is not always the same number of free (or noble) helpers who swear in the case of a common free (or noble) thief; rather, the oath-values of those swearing, added together, equal the thief's wergild</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">According to Liebermann the wergeld is that of the thief.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">126</biblScope></bibl><label>beo</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sie</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_1-1.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">126</biblScope></bibl><label>geladie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ladige</hi>. So.</seg></note>
      </div>
